<title>MALTA: Air Malta says plane hijacked to Germany.</title>
<headline>Air Malta says plane hijacked to Germany.</headline>
<dateline>VALLETTA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Air Malta Boeing 737 was diverted to Germany on a flight to Istanbul on Monday by a hijacker, a spokesman of the state-owned airline said.</p>
<p>Spokesman John Saliba said the situation on board the aircraft was &quot;reported to be calm&quot;. He said the flight was diverted to Cologne &quot;following a situation that developed on board and demands made by one of the passengers&quot;.  </p>
<p>Saliba said he had no information yet on what demands the lone hijacker had made.</p>
<p>The aircraft has 74 passengers and six crew on board, he said. Most of the passengers on this flight are usually not Maltese, he added.</p>
